      "body": "## Motivation\n\nInput top-k and token-ids logprobs (`return_logprob` with `logprob_start_len >= 0` plus `top_logprobs_num` or `token_ids_logprob`) blocked the overlap scheduler on the in-flight forward once per prefill (and per logprob chunk):\n\n- **Top-k:** results only went through async pinned copies when graph-pool borrowing was on (off by default). Otherwise they were read back with `.tolist()`.\n- **Token-ids:** the GPU logprobs were indexed with a Python list, an implicit synchronous H2D copy.\n\nThis affects `/v1/completions` with `echo` + `logprobs`, `/generate` prompt scoring, and setwise scoring in the Score API.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `layers/logprob_processor.py`: on CUDA, top-k / token-ids results always leave the device as async pinned copies with a copy-done event; borrowing now only decides where the scratch memory lives. The token-ids index is staged through `async_h2d`.\n- `finalize_input_logprobs()` already converts the pinned spans before every consumer reads them (prefill, disagg prefill, PP). Multi-item scoring and non-CUDA devices are unchanged.\n- `test_logprob_fast_input.py`: the test helper finalizes results the way the scheduler does.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nValues are computed exactly as before; only the D2H transport changes.\n\n- `test_logprob_fast_input.py` + `test_logprob_chunk_stitching.py`: 16 passed on H200.\n- `test/registered/core/test_srt_endpoint.py`: 20 passed, including all logprob tests.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nQwen3-0.6B, 1x H200, TP=1 bf16 with default flags, `main` vs this PR. 64 concurrent `/generate` requests with random prompts, `logprob_start_len=0`, 1 output token. Fresh server per run; two rounds each, numbers are the mean.\n\n| Workload | Before (req/s) | After (req/s) | Change | p50 latency |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| top-k=5, 1024-token prompt | 166 | 252 | +52% | 385 -> 252 ms |\n| top-k=5, 256-token prompt | 571 | 744 | +30% | 111 -> 85 ms |\n| token-ids (10 ids), 1024-token prompt | 187 | 236 | +26% | 342 -> 270 ms |\n| token-ids (10 ids), 256-token prompt | 602 | 685 | +14% | 106 -> 93 ms |\n| no logprobs (control) | 1683 | 1671 | ~0 | - |\n\nWith 256-token decode traffic sharing the server, top-k scoring throughput goes from 525 to 683 req/s (+30%).\n\nThe gain grows with prompt length (the removed `.tolist()` covered every prompt position) and is largest when the forward is short.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38901270197](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38901270197)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38901270193](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38901270193)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38901270116](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38901270116)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
